; ---------------------------------------------------------
; VNKit 2.12.1 — choices in the phone: a working reference
;
; Three proven patterns for choices in phone dialogues:
;   1) @chatActions — choice buttons INSIDE the chat screen.
;      They work while the script is parked at @phonehub / @waitchat;
;      the rest of the time the button bar is hidden (by design).
;   2) Branching inside the conversation: a branch hands out a NEW
;      @chatActions set (the command replaces the chat's whole list)
;      and returns to the hub via @chatend.
;   3) @choice inside a live dialogue (@online … goto:) —
;      choice buttons at the bottom of the chat, the player
;      never leaves the conversation (outside the phone @choice
;      is a full-screen overlay).
;
; Enable "Use Placeholder Graphics" to run this without any art.
; ---------------------------------------------------------

# Start

@bg Campus time:0.8
@phoneOn
@set affection.rin=0, trust.rin=0

; --- Chat history; both contacts come online.
; Rin has a LIVE dialogue waiting (goto:RinTalk), Max a short one.
@msg chat:rin notify:0 from:"Rin" "Found something in the archive. About «Elysium»."
@online chat:rin contact:"Rin 🌸" goto:RinTalk
@online chat:max contact:"Max 🎧" goto:MaxTalk notify:0

Rin is waiting for an answer. Open the phone (RMB) and enter her
chat — the live dialogue plays first.

; --- @waitchat: the script parks until Rin's live dialogue is done.
; The player may roam the phone meanwhile (Max's chat works too).
@waitchat rin

; --- PATTERN 1: choice buttons inside the chat.
; The live dialogue is over — the free phase begins. The buttons
; appear at the bottom of Rin's chat (and on her Contacts card).
; once:1 by default — each button fires once; do: changes
; relationship variables.
@chatActions chat:rin "Ask about the archive" goto:AskArchive do:affection.rin+=1 | "Promise to come" goto:PromiseRoof do:trust.rin+=1

; NOTE: there is deliberately no narration line between @waitchat and
; @phonehub — @chatend drops the player onto the chat list, and a line
; in chat mode would wait for them to re-enter the active chat. The hub
; opens right away: the player enters Rin's chat and sees the buttons.
; «Continue» sits on the chat list.
@phonehub

; --- After the free phase: react to what the player picked.
@if affection.rin > 0 goto:ChoseArchive
@if trust.rin > 0 goto:ChosePromise
You never answered Rin. She noticed.
@set trust.rin-=1
@goto Finale

# ChoseArchive
You took an interest in her find — that matters to Rin.
@goto Finale

# ChosePromise
You promised to come. Now you have to keep your word.

# Finale
@phone off
Classes are over. Tomorrow — the «Elysium» entrance test.
; (affection.rin / trust.rin are ready for further branching)

; =========================================================
; Rin's LIVE DIALOGUE — starts when the player enters her chat.
; PATTERN 3: @choice inside a dialogue — choice buttons right
; in the chat. Lines spoken by "Me" land in the chat as
; outgoing bubbles.
; =========================================================
# RinTalk
Rin: You read it?!
Me: Just opened the chat.
Rin: Tomorrow. Six o'clock. The roof. It's about «Elysium» — seriously.
@choice "I'll be there, promise" goto:RinPromise do:trust.rin+=2 | "I'll try, no promises" goto:RinMaybe

# RinPromise
Rin: Noted. Be late and I'll come find you.
@goto RinEnd

# RinMaybe
Rin: …Fine. Honest, at least.

# RinEnd
; @chatend finishes the live dialogue and returns the script
; to the hub (@waitchat / @phonehub) it started from.
@chatend

; --- Max's live dialogue: short, no choice (can be skipped).
# MaxTalk
Max: Yo. Music club after classes. You in?
Me: I'll drop by if I can.
Max: Do it. The drummer speeds up without you.
@chatend

; =========================================================
; CHOICE-BUTTON BRANCHES (patterns 1 and 2).
; Started by tapping a button in the chat; lines land in the
; chat as bubbles; @chatend returns the player to the hub.
; =========================================================
# AskArchive
Rin: The archive holds the selection lists. We were put there in advance.
Me: Who even needs this «Elysium»?
Rin: The ones who decide what we become after graduation.
; PATTERN 2: branching inside the conversation — REPLACE the button
; set with a new one. Anything not re-registered here disappears.
; if: shows the button only when the condition passes
; (affection.rin already grew from tapping "Ask about the archive").
@chatActions chat:rin "Ask to see the lists" goto:AskLists if:affection.rin>=1
@chatend

# AskLists
Rin: …Fine. Tomorrow, on the roof. Not a word to anyone.
@set trust.rin+=1
; The branch has fully played out — clear the chat's buttons.
@chatActions chat:rin clear:1
@chatend

# PromiseRoof
Me: I'll come. Six o'clock, the roof. On time.
Rin: We'll see.
@chatend
